{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB01168 - MONDO_20329",
  "verbalization": "Procarbazine is implicated in the pathogenesis of Classic Hodgkin Lymphoma, Lymphocyte-rich Type through a multi-step mechanism involving the induction of Hodgkin's Paragranuloma, a rare variant of Hodgkin's disease. This pathway is supported by the indication of Procarbazine in Hodgkin's Paragranuloma and the subsequent indication of Chlorambucil, which in turn is linked to the target disease. The presence of a direct indication from Procarbazine to Hodgkin's Paragranuloma suggests a potential role in the development of this rare subtype of Hodgkin's lymphoma. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism where Procarbazine may contribute to the progression of the disease through the activation of a cascade involving Hodgkin's Paragranuloma and subsequent chemotherapy agents. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link, though the exact molecular pathways remain to be fully elucidated.",
